  npcName: Waiter
  nodes:
  - nodeId: 0
    spanishLine: Nosotros ______ (tener) tres personas hoy.
    englishHint: 'Tener (To Have) follows these rules: Yo(I) - Tengo, Tu(You) - Tienes,
      El/Ella/Usted (He/She/You(formal)) - Tiene, Nosotros (We) - Tenemos, Ellos/Ellas/Ustedes
      (They/Them/You All) - Tienen. For this sentence what is the subject and use
      this list to find the correct conjugation. '
    options:
    - responseText: Tengo
      nextNodeId: 0
      endsConversation: 0
    - responseText: Tienes
      nextNodeId: 0
      endsConversation: 0
    - responseText: Tiene
      nextNodeId: 0
      endsConversation: 0
    - responseText: Tenemos
      nextNodeId: 1
      endsConversation: 0
    - responseText: Tienen
      nextNodeId: 0
      endsConversation: 0
  - nodeId: 1
    spanishLine: "\xBFD\xF3nde ________ (ser/estar) la mesa libre cerca de la ventana?"
    englishHint: 'Before conjugation which is the right verb ser or estar? Ser is
      for permanent being and Estar is for temporary being. Is location permanent
      or temporary (Hint: Be careful some things can move).  '
    options:
    - responseText: Ser
      nextNodeId: 1
      endsConversation: 0
    - responseText: Estar
      nextNodeId: 2
      endsConversation: 0
  - nodeId: 2
    spanishLine: "\xBFD\xF3nde ________ (estar) la mesa libre cerca de la ventana?"
    englishHint: 'Good job on identifying that its estar. Estar follows this pattern:
      Yo(I) - Estoy, Tu(You) - Estas, El/Ella/Usted (He/She/You(Formal) - Esta, Nosotros
      (We) - Estamos, Ellos/Ellas/Ustedes (They/Them/You All) - Estan. Here your
      subject is La Mesa which acccording to Spanish Grammar Rules is a singular
      she. Hence what is the right conjugation for she? '
    options:
    - responseText: Estoy
      nextNodeId: 2
      endsConversation: 0
    - responseText: Estas
      nextNodeId: 2
      endsConversation: 0
    - responseText: Esta
      nextNodeId: 3
      endsConversation: 0
    - responseText: 'Estamos '
      nextNodeId: 2
      endsConversation: 0
    - responseText: Estan
      nextNodeId: 2
      endsConversation: 0
  - nodeId: 3
    spanishLine: "\xA1Mira! En este momento, yo ________ ________ (estar + leer)
      el men\xFA del d\xEDa"
    englishHint: 'This sentence uses present progressive grammar. In English it would
      translate to I am reading. How would you say I am reading in Spanish? Leer
      Present Progressive: Yo(I) - Estoy Leyendo, Tu(You) - Estas Leyendo, El/Ella/Usted(He/She/You(Formal))
      - Esta Leyendo, Nosotros(We) - Estamos Leyendo, Ellos/Ellas/Ustedes(They/Them?You
      All) - Estan Leyendo. '
    options:
    - responseText: Estoy Leyendo
      nextNodeId: 4
      endsConversation: 0
    - responseText: Estas Leyendo
      nextNodeId: 3
      endsConversation: 0
    - responseText: Esta Leyendo
      nextNodeId: 3
      endsConversation: 0
    - responseText: Estamos Leyendo
      nextNodeId: 3
      endsConversation: 0
    - responseText: Estan Leyendo
      nextNodeId: 3
      endsConversation: 0
  - nodeId: 4
    spanishLine: "Yo ________ (tener) mucha hambre; yo ________ (querer) un s\xE1ndwich
      de jam\xF3n"
    englishHint: 'Tener: Yo(I) - Tengo, Tu(You) - Tienes, El/Ella/Usted (He/She/You(Formal))
      - Tiene, Nosotros(We) - Tenemos, Ellos/Ellas/Ustedes (They/Them/You All) -
      Tienen. Querer: Yo(I) - Quiero, Tu(You) - Quieres, El/Ella/Usted (He/She/You(Formal))
      - Quiere, Nosotros(We) - Queremos, Ellos/Ellas/Ustedes(They/Them/You All) -
      Quieren.  '
    options:
    - responseText: Tengo, Quiero
      nextNodeId: 5
      endsConversation: 0
    - responseText: Tienes, Quieres
      nextNodeId: 4
      endsConversation: 0
    - responseText: Tiene, Quiere
      nextNodeId: 4
      endsConversation: 0
    - responseText: Tenemos, Queremos
      nextNodeId: 4
      endsConversation: 0
    - responseText: Tienen, Queremos
      nextNodeId: 4
      endsConversation: 0
  - nodeId: 5
    spanishLine: "Ella ________ (tener) sed; ella ________ (preferir) un t\xE9 helado."
    englishHint: 'Tener - Yo(I) - Tengo, Tu(You) - Tienes, El/Ella/Usted(He/She/You(Formal))
      - Tiene, Nosotros(We) - Tenemos, Ellos/Ellas/Ustedes(They/Them/You All) - Tienen.
